<title>JAPAN: Japan May refined zinc imports slump 66 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan May refined zinc imports slump 66 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined zinc imports in May totalled 1,506 tonnes, down 65.8 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 May 97    April 97     May 96</p>
<p> Total		 1,506    115,982	 4,401</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Canada		  696	1,389	   594</p>
<p> North Korea	   414	  488	   364</p>
<p> China		   227     91,390	 2,173</p>
<p>Refined zinc imports in the first five months of calendar 1997 were 143,556 tonnes, up from 109,020 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Zinc imports usually surge in April due to the Generalised System of Preferences (GSP) which allows tariff exemptions for metal imports from designated developing countries.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
